    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3693\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to authorize Marie E. Abraham to take the\ncompetitive civil service examination and be placed on the eligible\nlist for appointment as a full-time police officer for the City of\nMechanicville, County of Saratoga\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nAuthorizes Marie E. Abraham to take the competitive exam for police\nofficer and be placed on the eligible list for such position in the\nCity of Mechanicville.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Authorizes Marie E. Abraham to sit for the civil service\nexam and be placed on the eligibility list for full time police\nofficer for the City of Mechanicville.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date as immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nDue to the provisions under the Civil Service Law, the City of\nMechanicville has requested legislation to permit one of their\npart-time officers, Marie E. Abraham, to be eligible to take the civil\nservice examination since she is currently older than 35 years old.\n\nRecruiting and retaining well-qualified full time police officers is\nchallenging for small and rural police departments. At the request of\nthe Mayor of the City of Mechanicville and the Chief of Police, and by\nresolution of the City Council, this bill would address this issue by\nallowing a part time police officer of the City of Mechanicville\nPolice Department to be eligible for full time status. While age\nrestrictions certainly have practical value, they do not always\nreflect the ability of some candidates to perform full time police\nduties. According to the Chief of Police, Officer Abraham (part time\nsince 2011) is perfectly competent to perform the duties required of a\nfull time police officer, rating her skills as \"exemplary\" even\noutperforming some of her younger coworkers.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
